# Coding Standards

## TypeScript

- Prefer `interface` for component props; `type` for unions and mapped types.
- Export components as `default` from feature files; named exports for hooks/utils.
- No `any`. Use `unknown` + narrowing at API boundaries.
- Import contract types from `projectos/contracts` via relative path (`../../../contracts/...`).

## React

- Functional components only. No class components.
- Props interface named `Props` when single component per file.
- Destructure with defaults in signature: `variant = 'primary'`.
- Side effects in `useEffect` with explicit deps; subscriptions must clean up.
- Prefer Zustand selectors over prop-drilling for cross-panel state.

## CSS Modules

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — token-driven, variant via module classes
<button className={`${styles.btn} ${styles[variant]} ${className}`} />

// ❌ BAD — inline styles for design tokens
<button style={{ background: '#161b22', borderRadius: 8 }} />
```

- Class order: base → variant → size → external `className`.
- Use `:focus-visible`, not `:focus`, for keyboard rings.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — never add infinite animations without a media-query guard.

## Accessibility

- Interactive elements: native `<button>`, `<a>`, or correct ARIA role + keyboard handler.
- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label` required.
- Glass overlays: maintain 4.5:1 text contrast on `--color-text-primary` backgrounds.
- Modals/menus: trap focus or use native focus management patterns.

## i18n

- User-visible strings via `useI18n()` / locale files — not inline English in JSX.
- Exception: developer-only debug labels behind `import.meta.env.DEV`.

## File Naming

- Components: `PascalCase.tsx` + `PascalCase.module.css`
- Hooks: `useThing.ts`
- One main component per file; sub-components only if tightly coupled and unexported.
